  "label": "Iranian Protests",
  "description": "The Iranian protests refer to a series of demonstrations that have occurred in Iran since 2022, primarily in response to the death of Mahsa Amini. These protests have been marked by widespread civil unrest, violence, and international attention. The image is a visual representation of the violence that has characterized these protests, and the meme's text, 'i forgot what are we fighting over again?', is a commentary on the ongoing nature of the conflict and the loss of life. Understanding the broader context of Iranian protests is essential to interpret the meme's reference to 'fighting' and the underlying social and political tensions.",
